Release packages contain, besides OpenDsec's own code (its LICENSE and this
NOTICE are in licenses/opendsec/; its source is the repository at the
release's tag), third-party software under its own licenses. Every release
carries these licenses in licenses/:

- licenses/go/: the Go standard library and the Go modules compiled into
  the OpenDsec binaries (Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT, MPL-2.0); the index there
  lists each module and version. MPL-2.0 modules are used unmodified.
- licenses/firecracker/: Firecracker and its jailer (Apache-2.0), shipped
  unmodified from the Firecracker project's release, with its NOTICE and
  THIRD-PARTY files.
- licenses/linux/: the Linux guest kernel (GPL-2.0 with the
  Linux-syscall-note), built from unmodified kernel.org sources. SOURCE.md
  there says where its complete corresponding source is: the kernel
  tarball, the exact configuration and the build script
  (deploy/guest-kernel in this repository).
